 ## Overview
-Implicit Surface Voxelization converts a mathematical implicit surface definition into a discrete voxel grid by rasterizing 2D rectangles within a Region of Interest (ROI) and evaluating the implicit function in the pixel shader [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from triangle-based rasterization methods (e.g., [Rasterization-based Voxelization](908-rasterization-based-voxelization.md)) by operating directly on analytical functions rather than polygonal approximations, allowing for the handling of complex, non-polygonal geometry [S1, S2, unofficial].
+Implicit Surface Voxelization converts a mathematical implicit surface definition into a discrete voxel representation by rasterizing 2D rectangles within a Region of Interest (ROI) and evaluating the implicit function in a pixel shader [S1, unofficial]. It differs from triangle-based rasterization methods (e.g., [Rasterization-based Voxelization](908-rasterization-based-voxelization.md)) by operating directly on analytical functions rather than polygonal approximations, allowing it to handle complex, non-polygonal geometry [S1, unofficial].
 
